WEBVTT

1
00:00.400 --> 00:03.470
Ask your IBM i in plain language.

2
00:03.520 --> 00:10.570
An open-source MCP server that lets Claude, Cursor and other AI assistants read Db2 for i.

3
00:11.170 --> 00:14.700
Start with a question that doesn't have a report yet.

4
00:16.400 --> 00:21.370
The server reads the table notes, then runs one read-only query.

5
00:22.870 --> 00:26.160
You get the answer, and the rows behind it.

6
00:27.560 --> 00:30.897
It reads only, and only what you allow:

7
00:30.947 --> 00:36.770
a read-only connection, an SQL validator, and a library allowlist.

8
00:37.370 --> 00:40.280
Nothing new to install on the IBM i.

9
00:40.330 --> 00:45.460
It connects through the host servers you already run, or over SSH.

10
00:47.010 --> 00:49.180
Read-only by design.
